  "notes": "Not transcribed from the 1993 paper, which is not available online; the URL points to a survey that cites it. The skew block is a union of nine cosets of H = <2> (one from each pair {alpha_{2i}, alpha_{2i+1}}) and each symmetric block is {0} with four pairs, the ansatz of Djokovic 2009, Section 5.7. An exhaustive search over this ansatz finds 18 solutions in a single equiv-v1 class. The rows are stored in canonical form under equiv-v1."
